      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While chaos theory explains how minor fluctuations can lead to major market shifts, there is currently no empirical evidence or mathematical basis to support the idea that human mental coherence can generate measurable trading signals or directly trigger HFT algorithms. Algorithmic models operate on quantitative data feed inputs, not on the subjective cognitive states of human observers, so the \"internal\" state of a trader's focus does not function as a computational input within the market infrastructure. It is more likely that the perceived \"synchronicity\" you experienced is a cognitive illusion caused by the brain's tendency to find patterns (pareidolia) in the inherent randomness of high-frequency noise, rather than a genuine external feedback loop created by your awareness.",
      "source": "target",
